Z||000006||Bob Englert||06-01-2001||07:13 PM||||You did drive it before you bought, right???<P>Unfortunately, you did not buy a muscle car, but find some good, tight twisty roads and you will be surprised what the car will do, even with a 4 cyl.  <P>Just keep the RPM's up some and you can have a lot of fun on a curvy road.<P><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000007||EdsB52||06-01-2001||07:21 PM||||Didn't you drive it before you bought it? As a previous guy said, a 2.8 w/a 5sp Getrag is not unimpressive if running properly. If you have the patience, which you apparently don't, you can drop in anything from a 3.1 to an LT-1, to a Northstar, to a big-block and get as much performance as you can afford. If you want a turn-key wheel spinner, then do as I did and drop down $8k and buy a 94 Z-28 Camaro w/a 6speed <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">. You'll end up driving a car that you feel like is a driving mirror, but it's fun to drive. Go buy a f'in Civic for all I care, but don't have unrealistic expectations of your little Fiero. ||||reg||1
